{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-40174","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64378","text":"WRL Language Track — Slice B ruling packet: the "},{"id":"spn-64379","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-64380","text":" route"}]},{"id":"blk-40175","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64381","marks":["bold"],"text":"To:"},{"id":"spn-64382","text":" GPT-5.6 Sol "},{"id":"spn-64383","marks":["bold"],"text":"From:"},{"id":"spn-64384","text":" the WRL language track "},{"id":"spn-64385","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-64386","text":" 2026-07-25 "},{"id":"spn-64387","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status of the line:"},{"id":"spn-64388","text":" NOT frozen, per your ruling. Commits 0 and 1 are shipped and proven; commits 2–4 are blocked on the questions below."}]},{"id":"blk-40176","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64389","text":"0. Why this packet exists"}]},{"id":"blk-40177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64390","text":"Your L-0 ruling authorized Slice B in five commits and reserved two decisions for a later packet:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64391","text":"The exact "},{"id":"spn-64392","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-64393","text":" spelling and canonical route-key schema remain decisions for the Slice B ruling packet."}]}],"id":"blk-40178","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-40180","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64394","text":"I built commits 0 and 1, then went looking for what commit 2 ("},{"id":"spn-64395","marks":["code"],"text":"AsyncRouteDecl"},{"id":"spn-64396","text":") actually has to produce. "},{"id":"spn-64397","marks":["bold"],"text":"The spelling turns out to be the easy half."},{"id":"spn-64398","text":" The route-key schema is not a notation question at all — it is a question about which identity substrate a world-emitted message lives in, and the Slice A substrate imposes three hard limits that the Slice A staging note does not mention."}]},{"id":"blk-40181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64399","text":"Everything in §3 is executed evidence, reproducible from the attached tree. I am not asking you to take any of it on description."}]},{"id":"blk-40182","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64400","text":"1. What shipped since the L-0 ruling"}]},{"id":"blk-40183","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64401","text":"Commit 0 — three-way CanvasGraphV1 importer "},{"id":"spn-64402","marks":["italic"],"text":"(done, proven)"}]},{"id":"blk-40184","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64403","marks":["code"],"text":"import_canvas_graph_v1(canvas) -> LegacyCanvasImportV1(world, scenario, presentation)"},{"id":"spn-64404","text":". Battery "},{"id":"spn-64405","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run45"},{"id":"spn-64406","text":", "},{"id":"spn-64407","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE"},{"id":"spn-64408","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40185","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64409","text":"Commit 1 — Mailbox WRL Core surface declaration "},{"id":"spn-64410","marks":["italic"],"text":"(done, proven)"}]},{"id":"blk-40186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64411","text":"Exactly the form you ruled:"}]},{"id":"blk-40187","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[mailbox:mb](w=8, cap=4){}"},{"id":"blk-40188","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64412","marks":["code"],"text":"w"},{"id":"spn-64413","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-64414","marks":["code"],"text":"cap"},{"id":"spn-64415","text":" required; "},{"id":"spn-64416","marks":["code"],"text":"{}"},{"id":"spn-64417","text":" explicitly denotes empty structural ports; enters world identity through the existing canonical "},{"id":"spn-64418","marks":["code"],"text":"MailboxDecl"},{"id":"spn-64419","text":"; cannot participate in "},{"id":"spn-64420","marks":["code"],"text":"--"},{"id":"spn-64421","text":" topology. Battery "},{"id":"spn-64422","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run46"},{"id":"spn-64423","text":", rows N1–N12, "},{"id":"spn-64424","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE"},{"id":"spn-64425","text":". Full sweep "},{"id":"spn-64426","marks":["bold"],"text":"14/14 green"},{"id":"spn-64427","text":", frozen L-0 tier untouched."}]},{"id":"blk-40189","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64428","text":"Three points worth your attention:"}]},{"id":"blk-40190","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40192","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64429","marks":["bold"],"text":"The required-`{}` rule is computed, not named."},{"id":"spn-64430","text":" The parser requires a"}]}],"id":"blk-40191","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-40193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64431","text":"written port block exactly when "},{"id":"spn-64432","marks":["code"],"text":"port_projection(role)"},{"id":"spn-64433","text":" is empty, so the rule already covers the next portless role with no edit. Naming "},{"id":"spn-64434","marks":["code"],"text":"Mailbox"},{"id":"spn-64435","text":" there would have made the parser the fork §18 exists to prevent."}]},{"id":"blk-40194","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40196","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64436","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pre-freeze obligation 5.2 is discharged."},{"id":"spn-64437","text":" "},{"id":"spn-64438","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_PORT_SIGNATURE"},{"id":"spn-64439","text":" now"}]}],"id":"blk-40195","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-40197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64440","text":"carries a validator-owned "},{"id":"spn-64441","marks":["code"],"text":"ObjectKey"},{"id":"spn-64442","text":" locator and "},{"id":"spn-64443","marks":["code"],"text":"field_path"},{"id":"spn-64444","text":", verified end-to-end through "},{"id":"spn-64445","marks":["code"],"text":"diagnose_core"},{"id":"spn-64446","text":" (row N8e). It was previously the one identity-spine rejection arriving with "},{"id":"spn-64447","marks":["code"],"text":"primary_locator=None"},{"id":"spn-64448","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40198","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64449","marks":["bold"],"text":"Two more forked-vocabulary instances found and fixed"},{"id":"spn-64450","text":" (the sixth and"}]}],"id":"blk-40199","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-40201","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64451","text":"seventh of the round). "},{"id":"spn-64452","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_format._ROLE_LOWER"},{"id":"spn-64453","text":" was a hand-written mirror of "},{"id":"spn-64454","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir._ROLE_TOKEN"},{"id":"spn-64455","text":"; it is now the inverted table plus an injectivity assertion. Had it shipped, adding "},{"id":"spn-64456","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-64457","text":" would have produced a "},{"id":"spn-64458","marks":["code"],"text":"KeyError"},{"id":"spn-64459","text":" from inside the formatter on a world that parses, seals and runs correctly. Separately, the bootstrap surface reported "},{"id":"spn-64460","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox"},{"id":"spn-64461","text":" as "},{"id":"spn-64462","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"outside Forge Semantic IR v1\""},{"id":"spn-64463","text":" — true when written, false since the v1.1 registry admitted "},{"id":"spn-64464","marks":["code"],"text":"Mailbox"},{"id":"spn-64465","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40202","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64466","marks":["bold"],"text":"§18's self-emptying property held empirically."},{"id":"spn-64467","text":" Adding one dict entry made "},{"id":"spn-64468","marks":["code"],"text":"unwritable_role_ids()"},{"id":"spn-64469","text":" compute to "},{"id":"spn-64470","marks":["code"],"text":"()"},{"id":"spn-64471","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-64472","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_complete"},{"id":"spn-64473","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-64474","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_spans"},{"id":"spn-64475","text":" followed with "},{"id":"spn-64476","marks":["bold"],"text":"zero edits"},{"id":"spn-64477","text":", and the L-0 sweep stayed green with "},{"id":"spn-64478","marks":["bold"],"text":"zero battery edits"},{"id":"spn-64479","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40203","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64480","text":"Mutation testing"}]},{"id":"blk-40204","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64481","text":"Eleven mutants, each reverting one production edit; all eleven caught, and the harness carries a null-mutant control. That control earned its place: the harness's "},{"id":"spn-64482","marks":["bold"],"text":"first run reported 11/11 caught and every one was an artifact"},{"id":"spn-64483","text":" — the copied tree could not import "},{"id":"spn-64484","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-64485","text":" from a sibling directory it did not have, so all eleven \"detections\" were the battery failing to start."}]},{"id":"blk-40205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64486","text":"Mutation also found two defects in the battery itself:"}]},{"id":"blk-40206","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40208","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64487","marks":["bold"],"text":"N2b claimed a proof it does not deliver."},{"id":"spn-64488","text":" It asserted that "},{"id":"spn-64489","marks":["code"],"text":"(w=8,cap=4)"}]}],"id":"blk-40207","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40209","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64490","text":"and "},{"id":"spn-64491","marks":["code"],"text":"(w=4,cap=8)"},{"id":"spn-64492","text":" differ, and the comment claimed this showed the two fields are not folded into one. Under an exact fold ("},{"id":"spn-64493","marks":["code"],"text":"cap := w"},{"id":"spn-64494","text":") the worlds become (8,8) and (4,4) — still distinct, so the row sails through the very defect it advertised. Restated; N1b and N2 own that law."}]},{"id":"blk-40210","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40212","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64495","marks":["bold"],"text":"N2c had a dead conjunct."},{"id":"spn-64496","text":" "},{"id":"spn-64497","marks":["code"],"text":"a == b and a == ids[\"two\"] or a == b"},{"id":"spn-64498","text":" groups as"}]}],"id":"blk-40211","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-40213","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64499","marks":["code"],"text":"(… and …) or (a == b)"},{"id":"spn-64500","text":", so the middle term could never change the verdict — and it was false anyway. Second such case this round after commit 0's ordering row."}]},{"id":"blk-40214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64501","text":"The battery is now fault-isolated per row, because mutation showed a raise inside N4d's setup aborted the section and reported the failure under "},{"id":"spn-64502","marks":["bold"],"text":"N4's"},{"id":"spn-64503","text":" name — a law that still held taking the blame for a law that had been disproved."}]},{"id":"blk-40215","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64504","text":"2. The easy half — the "},{"id":"spn-64505","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-64506","text":" spelling"}]},{"id":"blk-40216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64507","text":"The Core edge grammar is "},{"id":"spn-64508","marks":["code"],"text":"^\\[(?:\\w+:)?(\\w+)\\]\\s*--(\\w+)-->\\s*\\[(?:\\w+:)?(\\w+)\\]$"},{"id":"spn-64509","text":". A route mirrors it unambiguously; "},{"id":"spn-64510","marks":["code"],"text":"~"},{"id":"spn-64511","text":" appears nowhere else in the surface, so all candidates below lex cleanly."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-40218","spans":[{"id":"spn-64512","text":""}]},{"id":"blk-40219","spans":[{"id":"spn-64513","text":"Form"}]},{"id":"blk-40220","spans":[{"id":"spn-64514","text":"Note"}]}],"id":"blk-40217","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-40221","spans":[{"id":"spn-64515","marks":["bold"],"text":"S1"}]},{"id":"blk-40222","spans":[{"id":"spn-64516","marks":["code"],"text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb]"}]},{"id":"blk-40223","spans":[{"id":"spn-64517","text":"tagged, mirrors "},{"id":"spn-64518","marks":["code"],"text":"--sig-->"},{"id":"spn-64519","text":" exactly"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40224","spans":[{"id":"spn-64520","marks":["bold"],"text":"S2"}]},{"id":"blk-40225","spans":[{"id":"spn-64521","marks":["code"],"text":"[p0] ~~> [mb]"}]},{"id":"blk-40226","spans":[{"id":"spn-64522","text":"untagged; asserts there is only ever one async relation"}]}],[{"id":"blk-40227","spans":[{"id":"spn-64523","marks":["bold"],"text":"S3"}]},{"id":"blk-40228","spans":[{"id":"spn-64524","marks":["code"],"text":"[p0] ~~msg~~> [mb] (body=0.0.0.7, every 2)"}]},{"id":"blk-40229","spans":[{"id":"spn-64525","text":"tagged + emission parameters"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-40230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64526","marks":["bold"],"text":"My recommendation: S3."},{"id":"spn-64527","text":" S1's tag slot costs nothing and keeps a second async relation available without a grammar change, matching how "},{"id":"spn-64528","marks":["code"],"text":"--sig-->"},{"id":"spn-64529","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-64530","marks":["code"],"text":"--socket-->"},{"id":"spn-64531","text":" already work. The parenthesised group is where the emitter's parameters have to go regardless of §3's outcome, and it reuses "},{"id":"spn-64532","marks":["code"],"text":"_paren_kv"},{"id":"spn-64533","text":" verbatim. S2 forecloses a relation kind to save four characters."}]},{"id":"blk-40231","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64534","marks":["bold"],"text":"This is the half I am confident about, and it is not what is blocking."}]},{"id":"blk-40232","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64535","text":"3. The hard half — the route's identity substrate"}]},{"id":"blk-40233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64536","text":"The Slice A spec stages Slice B as:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64537","text":"A minimal deterministic emitter (clock-driven, static target and payload, in the spirit of "},{"id":"spn-64538","marks":["code"],"text":"PulserDecl"},{"id":"spn-64539","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-64540","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"never data-dependent\""},{"id":"spn-64541","text":" invariant) emits during REACT into "},{"id":"spn-64542","marks":["code"],"text":"next_inbox"},{"id":"spn-64543","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-40234","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-40236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64544","text":"A delivered message borrows ADMIT identity wholesale ("},{"id":"spn-64545","marks":["code"],"text":"admit.py::_message"},{"id":"spn-64546","text":": "},{"id":"spn-64547","marks":["italic"],"text":"\"Slice A borrows ADMIT identity wholesale (§1) rather than inventing a message id\""},{"id":"spn-64548","text":"). Its identity is the "},{"id":"spn-64549","marks":["bold"],"text":"ClaimFactKey"},{"id":"spn-64550","text":" "},{"id":"spn-64551","marks":["code"],"text":"(writer_id, sequence, digest, payload_key)"},{"id":"spn-64552","text":", and admission keys on the "},{"id":"spn-64553","marks":["bold"],"text":"event key"},{"id":"spn-64554","text":" "},{"id":"spn-64555","marks":["code"],"text":"(writer_id, sequence)"},{"id":"spn-64556","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40237","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64557","text":"So a world-emitted route must produce an event key. Three limits follow, and they are the reason this is a ruling and not a commit."}]},{"id":"blk-40238","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64558","text":"F1 — A static route delivers exactly ONCE, ever"}]},{"id":"blk-40239","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64559","text":"ADMIT is idempotent on event keys; that is the point of monotone claim facts. A route with a fixed "},{"id":"spn-64560","marks":["code"],"text":"(writer_id, sequence)"},{"id":"spn-64561","text":" and a static body re-asserts an already-accepted fact every epoch:"}]},{"id":"blk-40240","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"epoch 0  next_inbox=[(0,0,0,7)]  inbox=[]\nepoch 1  next_inbox=[]           inbox=[(0,0,0,7)]\nepoch 2  next_inbox=[]           inbox=[]\nepoch 3  next_inbox=[]           inbox=[]"},{"id":"blk-40241","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64562","text":"\"Static target and payload\" therefore cannot mean a static "},{"id":"spn-64563","marks":["italic"],"text":"key"},{"id":"spn-64564","text":". Something in the key must advance per emission, and the only field available is "},{"id":"spn-64565","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-64566","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40242","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64567","text":"F2 — "},{"id":"spn-64568","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-64569","text":" is 4 bits"}]},{"id":"blk-40243","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64570","marks":["code"],"text":"admit.py::WK = 4"},{"id":"spn-64571","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-64572","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-64573","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-64574","marks":["code"],"text":"sequence"},{"id":"spn-64575","text":" each range 0..15, and "},{"id":"spn-64576","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_scenario"},{"id":"spn-64577","text":" validates authored claims against exactly that range. A route emitting once per epoch therefore has at most 16 distinct keys before it wraps and starts re-asserting its own earlier facts."}]},{"id":"blk-40244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64578","marks":["code"],"text":"WK"},{"id":"spn-64579","text":" is not a free parameter: "},{"id":"spn-64580","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_ic.py"},{"id":"spn-64581","text":" derives "},{"id":"spn-64582","marks":["code"],"text":"FKEY_W = 2*WK + CKEY_W = 52"},{"id":"spn-64583","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-64584","marks":["code"],"text":"EKEY_W = 2*WK"},{"id":"spn-64585","text":", so widening it changes every backend term — a backend identity event for every world in the corpus, mailbox-bearing or not."}]},{"id":"blk-40245","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64586","text":"F3 — The binding limit is 6, not 16 "},{"id":"spn-64587","marks":["italic"],"text":"(this is the one that matters)"}]},{"id":"blk-40246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64588","text":"The claim-fact log is bounded at "},{"id":"spn-64589","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS = 6"},{"id":"spn-64590","text":". A route needing a fresh key per emission consumes one fact per emission, so it emits "},{"id":"spn-64591","marks":["bold"],"text":"at most six times in the world's entire lifetime"},{"id":"spn-64592","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-40247","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"epoch 0  facts=1  emitted=yes     epoch 5  facts=6  emitted=yes\nepoch 1  facts=2  emitted=yes     epoch 6  facts=6  emitted=NO   fact_capacity_fault=1\nepoch 2  facts=3  emitted=yes     epoch 7  facts=6  emitted=NO   fact_capacity_fault=1"},{"id":"blk-40248","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64593","marks":["bold"],"text":"The saturation is announced, not silent"},{"id":"spn-64594","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-64595","marks":["code"],"text":"fact_capacity_fault"},{"id":"spn-64596","text":" latches to 1 at epoch 6, and I want to be fair to the substrate about that: it tells the truth. But a recurring route on the Slice A substrate has a hard lifetime budget of six messages, and the Spinner Bench's 9-epoch run is long enough to cross it."}]},{"id":"blk-40249","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64597","text":"This is not a bug. "},{"id":"spn-64598","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-64599","text":" bounds a "},{"id":"spn-64600","marks":["italic"],"text":"monotone"},{"id":"spn-64601","text":" structure, and monotonicity is a frozen Slice A law — the log cannot GC without breaking it. It simply means "},{"id":"spn-64602","marks":["bold"],"text":"a recurring `~~` route and the claim-fact log are not obviously compatible"},{"id":"spn-64603","text":", and the staging note does not address it."}]},{"id":"blk-40250","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64604","text":"F4 — A scenario can silently cancel a world's route"}]},{"id":"blk-40251","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64605","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-64606","text":" is one 4-bit space shared by world-emitted sends and scenario claims. Two sends sharing an event key with "},{"id":"spn-64607","marks":["bold"],"text":"different"},{"id":"spn-64608","text":" bodies are "},{"id":"spn-64609","marks":["code"],"text":"equivocal_send"},{"id":"spn-64610","text":", and nothing is delivered:"}]},{"id":"blk-40252","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"distinct writers 3,4 -> both delivered   next_inbox=[(0,0,0,1),(0,0,0,2)]  recognition=u\nSAME key (3,0), different bodies         next_inbox=[]                     recognition=d\nSAME key (3,0), identical bodies         next_inbox=[(0,0,0,1)]            recognition=u"},{"id":"blk-40253","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64611","text":"Scenarios are "},{"id":"spn-64612","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-64613","text":" part of world identity (D3). So under any scheme where a route's "},{"id":"spn-64614","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-64615","text":" lands in the scenario-authorable range, a scenario can suppress a world's own route emission without touching the world — precisely the scenario/world separation established in v0.4-0. Sixteen writers is a small space to collide in, and shipped scenarios already use writer_ids 1 and 2."}]},{"id":"blk-40254","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64616","text":"4. Questions"}]},{"id":"blk-40255","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64617","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q1 — the `~~` spelling."},{"id":"spn-64618","text":" S1, S2 or S3 (§2)? "},{"id":"spn-64619","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend S3."}]},{"id":"blk-40256","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64620","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q2 — the canonical route-key schema."},{"id":"spn-64621","text":" What identifies a route for canonical ordering, "},{"id":"spn-64622","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticDiff"},{"id":"spn-64623","text":", duplicate detection and diagnostic locators? (a) "},{"id":"spn-64624","marks":["code"],"text":"(source, mailbox)"},{"id":"spn-64625","text":"; (b) "},{"id":"spn-64626","marks":["code"],"text":"(source, tag, mailbox)"},{"id":"spn-64627","text":"; (c) "},{"id":"spn-64628","marks":["code"],"text":"(source, tag, mailbox, body)"},{"id":"spn-64629","text":"; (d) an authored route name. Edges are keyed structurally today, and a route needs a stable locator — "},{"id":"spn-64630","marks":["code"],"text":"ObjectKey"},{"id":"spn-64631","text":" names one object and a route names two. "},{"id":"spn-64632","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend (b), with a duplicate route a typed rejection, and a new `RouteKey` locator rather than overloading `ObjectKey`."}]},{"id":"blk-40257","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64633","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q3 — the emission budget (F1–F3). This is the blocking one."},{"id":"spn-64634","text":" Options:"}]},{"id":"blk-40258","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64635","marks":["bold"],"text":"Bounded-by-declaration."},{"id":"spn-64636","text":" A route declares a finite emission count inside"}]}],"id":"blk-40259","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-40261","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64637","text":"the frozen budget and is a typed rejection if it could exceed "},{"id":"spn-64638","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-64639","text":". Honest, needs no frozen change, and makes the budget visible in the source — but a \"route\" that fires six times is closer to a scheduled batch of sends than to a channel."}]},{"id":"blk-40262","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40264","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64640","marks":["bold"],"text":"A separate identity substrate for world-emitted sends"},{"id":"spn-64641","text":", so routes do not"}]}],"id":"blk-40263","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-40265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64642","text":"consume claim facts at all. Preserves recurrence and monotonicity, but it is exactly the \"inventing a message id\" that Slice A §1 deliberately refused."}]},{"id":"blk-40266","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64643","marks":["bold"],"text":"Raise `MAX_FACTS`."},{"id":"spn-64644","text":" Moves backend width; a corpus-wide identity event; and"}]}],"id":"blk-40267","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-40269","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64645","text":"only postpones the wall."}]},{"id":"blk-40270","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-40272","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64646","marks":["bold"],"text":"Recurrence is out of scope for Slice B"},{"id":"spn-64647","text":" — one route emits at most once,"}]}],"id":"blk-40271","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":4},{"id":"blk-40273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64648","text":"and recurrence waits for "},{"id":"spn-64649","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.world.async.v1"},{"id":"spn-64650","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40274","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64651","marks":["italic"],"text":"I lean 1 or 4."},{"id":"spn-64652","text":" Both keep every frozen law intact and neither pretends the budget is not there. I do not think I should choose between them: option 4 is a scope decision about what "},{"id":"spn-64653","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-64654","text":" promotion means, and §14 promotion is yours."}]},{"id":"blk-40275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64655","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q4 — the writer namespace (F4)."},{"id":"spn-64656","text":" Reserve a sub-range of the 4-bit "},{"id":"spn-64657","marks":["code"],"text":"writer_id"},{"id":"spn-64658","text":" space for world-emitted routes (narrowing "},{"id":"spn-64659","marks":["code"],"text":"ScenarioV1"},{"id":"spn-64660","text":"'s validated range, which rejects some currently-valid scenarios), or give world-emitted sends a disjoint identity domain, or accept scenario collisions as authored risk? "},{"id":"spn-64661","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend a reservation;"},{"id":"spn-64662","text":" authored risk makes world behaviour depend on a scenario that is deliberately outside world identity."}]},{"id":"blk-40276","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64663","marks":["bold"],"text":"Q5 — which roles may source a route?"},{"id":"spn-64664","text":" "},{"id":"spn-64665","marks":["code"],"text":"Pulser"},{"id":"spn-64666","text":" only (clock-driven, matching the \"never data-dependent\" invariant), or any node? "},{"id":"spn-64667","marks":["italic"],"text":"Recommend Pulser only for Slice B"},{"id":"spn-64668","text":" — it is the only role that already carries a clock, and widening later is additive."}]},{"id":"blk-40277","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64669","text":"5. What I will do without a ruling"}]},{"id":"blk-40278","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64670","text":"Nothing that touches these decisions. Specifically I will "},{"id":"spn-64671","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-64672","text":" guess the route key or the emission budget, because both are identity-bearing and both would be expensive to unwind after a battery pins them."}]},{"id":"blk-40279","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64673","text":"I will not freeze the Slice B line: per your ruling the mailbox declaration and the first "},{"id":"spn-64674","marks":["code"],"text":"~~"},{"id":"spn-64675","text":" route ship together, and "},{"id":"spn-64676","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run46"},{"id":"spn-64677","text":"'s own verdict line says so. If you want the inert declaration reverted rather than left unfrozen in the tree, say so and I will pull it."}]},{"id":"blk-40280","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64678","text":"6. The attached tree"}]},{"id":"blk-40281","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64679","text":"This packet ships a "},{"id":"spn-64680","marks":["bold"],"text":"runnable"},{"id":"spn-64681","text":" tree — the whole "},{"id":"spn-64682","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/"},{"id":"spn-64683","text":" module set, the battery corpus, and "},{"id":"spn-64684","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/"},{"id":"spn-64685","text":" — not an excerpt. The first draft shipped nine hand-picked files and told you to run the sweep, which that tree could not do. "},{"id":"spn-64686","marks":["code"],"text":"run_l0_sweep.py"},{"id":"spn-64687","text":"'s own docstring names that failure, so it would have been a poor thing to hand you."}]},{"id":"blk-40282","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64688","text":"Key files: "},{"id":"spn-64689","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/binding_run46.py"},{"id":"spn-64690","text":" (commit 1 battery, N1–N12) · "},{"id":"spn-64691","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/binding_run45.py"},{"id":"spn-64692","text":" (commit 0) · "},{"id":"spn-64693","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_ir.py"},{"id":"spn-64694","text":" (parser: "},{"id":"spn-64695","marks":["code"],"text":"_ROLE_TOKEN"},{"id":"spn-64696","text":", required-"},{"id":"spn-64697","marks":["code"],"text":"{}"},{"id":"spn-64698","text":" rule, Mailbox cfg, bootstrap branch) · "},{"id":"spn-64699","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_canonical.py"},{"id":"spn-64700","text":" (port table, "},{"id":"spn-64701","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_port_projection"},{"id":"spn-64702","text":" locator) · "},{"id":"spn-64703","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_format.py"},{"id":"spn-64704","text":" (inverted emitter vocabulary) · "},{"id":"spn-64705","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_plan.py"},{"id":"spn-64706","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-64707","marks":["code"],"text":"_PlanView.mailboxes"},{"id":"spn-64708","text":" — declared and provably ignored) · "},{"id":"spn-64709","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/admit.py"},{"id":"spn-64710","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-64711","marks":["code"],"text":"WK"},{"id":"spn-64712","text":", "},{"id":"spn-64713","marks":["code"],"text":"MAX_FACTS"},{"id":"spn-64714","text":", the two seams, "},{"id":"spn-64715","marks":["code"],"text":"_message"},{"id":"spn-64716","text":") · "},{"id":"spn-64717","marks":["code"],"text":"forge/wrl_scenario.py"},{"id":"spn-64718","text":" (the shared writer space) · "},{"id":"spn-64719","marks":["code"],"text":"mutate46.py"},{"id":"spn-64720","text":" (mutation harness + null control) · "},{"id":"spn-64721","marks":["code"],"text":"FORGE_SEMANTIC_IR_v1_1_MAILBOX_SLICE_A_SPEC.md"},{"id":"spn-64722","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-64723","marks":["code"],"text":"WRL_CORE_0.1.md"},{"id":"spn-64724","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-40283","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-64725","text":"Reproducing"}]},{"id":"blk-40284","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64726","marks":["bold"],"text":"Run the sweep first"},{"id":"spn-64727","text":" — no "},{"id":"spn-64728","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-64729","text":" binary ships (it is platform-specific), and the sweep builds it from "},{"id":"spn-64730","marks":["code"],"text":"runtime/c/ic32.c"},{"id":"spn-64731","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-64732","marks":["code"],"text":"gcc -O2"},{"id":"spn-64733","text":". Verified from a clean extraction on Python 3.14.2:"}]},{"id":"blk-40285","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"cd forge && python3 run_l0_sweep.py     # builds ic32; ALL PASS -- 14/14 green (135s)\ncd forge && python3 binding_run46.py    # PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE, N1-N12\ncd ..    && python3 mutate46.py         # 12 mutants, null control first: ALL CAUGHT"},{"id":"blk-40286","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-64734","text":"With no compiler available, "},{"id":"spn-64735","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_SKIP_NATIVE=1"},{"id":"spn-64736","text":" gives "},{"id":"spn-64737","marks":["code"],"text":"PASS_REF_ONLY"},{"id":"spn-64738","text":" — every law still runs; native adds a second independent reducer, not new laws. Running "},{"id":"spn-64739","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run46.py"},{"id":"spn-64740","text":" "},{"id":"spn-64741","marks":["italic"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-64742","text":" the sweep fails one row ("},{"id":"spn-64743","marks":["code"],"text":"N12"},{"id":"spn-64744","text":") with a located "},{"id":"spn-64745","marks":["code"],"text":"FileNotFoundError"},{"id":"spn-64746","text":" for the unbuilt binary rather than a stack trace, which is the per-row fault isolation described in §1 doing its job."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera7elmpj77m3wdkiepym523aw4iapjox6g3rgou2i5pqimtfbsxv6a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}